The only case where it would actually benefit the player is when the
monster is given a wish that wouldn't have existed before, i.e. from a
smoky potion. This is an extremely rare event. If a monster gets a
hold of a wand of wishes then _at best_ the monster will wish for what
the player would have wished for (and the player still has to pry it
from the monster's cold, dead fingers). So I don't see how this would
make life easier for the player.

Unless, of course, the player is trying to achieve wishless conduct
and hands smoky potions and wands of wishes to monsters in the hope
that they will do the dirty work for her. One way around this is to
have monsters almost always wish for objects that are useful for
monsters but not nearly as useful (as a wish) for players:
(some ideas from Roger Broadbent)
wand of digging
wand of create monster
cursed scroll of teleportation
cursed scroll of create monster
cockatrice eggs (do monsters throw eggs?)
amulet of life saving (the player usually wouldn't be able to get this
one off the monster)

Or maybe the whole idea won't work. It is rather cruel to let monsters
use up that wand of wishes before you get to it, especially for less
experienced players.

